<title>LUXEMBOURG: Syndicate guarantees EIB loan for Slovak energy.</title>
<headline>Syndicate guarantees EIB loan for Slovak energy.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>An international syndicate of 11 European, Japanese and U.S. banks has guaranteed a European Investment Bank loan of 70 million European currency units to the Slovak power utility, the EIB said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The loan will be made to Slovenske Elektrarne for the refurbishment of new boilers, steam turbines and transformers, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The EIB said the loan reflected a growing move to lend money backed by commercial banks.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newroom +32 2 287 6830</p>
</text>
